<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>. ValidationRule.Description is
        capped at 255 characters; a comment is repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata
        API. It must sit INSIDE the root element. A comment placed ABOVE <ValidationRule>
        breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent xml
        file" error.

        =====================================================================================
        ADDED 2026-08-20 (Tranche 2, Workstream A4). THE ONE PATH SPECIFIC RULE ON THIS
        OBJECT. The other three A4 rules here are arithmetic invariants; this one is a
        TRANSITION GATE, and it is shaped differently on purpose.
        Shared object level rationale: Counter_Price_Is_Positive.validationRule-meta.xml.
        =====================================================================================
        An LOI that has been EXECUTED without a final agreed price is a signed deal with no
        number in it. Final_Agreed_Price__c is what feeds the Opportunity Amount and the
        Transaction purchase price downstream, so a blank one at the terminal stage silently
        propagates a null into the money columns of everything after it.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 'Executed', NOT 'Signed'. NAMING THE VALUE IS WHAT SCOPES THIS RULE TO THE
        DISPOSITION PATH, AND IT IS STRONGER THAN A RECORD TYPE TEST.
        =====================================================================================
        LOI__c is dual record type. 'Executed' is the DISPOSITION terminal; 'Signed' is the
        ACQUISITION terminal. An acquisition LOI can never carry 'Executed', so this rule is
        structurally unreachable from the acquisition path without any record type criterion
        at all. That is the same technique Tranche 2's NDA latch fix uses (branching on
        'Declined', which only Disposition_NDA exposes) and it is preferred here for the two
        reasons recorded in Broker_Lookup_Is_Off_Market_Only and NdaSelector.queryExpiryAlerts:
        a value named rule survives a record type rename, and it does not depend on rows
        having been migrated off the Master record type.
        🔴 DO NOT "HARMONISE" THIS WITH THE ACQUISITION TERMINAL BY ADDING 'Signed' TO THE
        TEST. Acquisition LOIs reach 'Signed' through an approval process that this rule has
        never gated, and adding it would block a live acquisition workflow. If the acquisition
        side ever needs the same guarantee it needs its OWN rule, argued on its own facts.
        ⚠ ONE OVERLAP EXISTS ON THIS FIELD AND IT IS NOT THIS VALUE: 'Under Review' is carried
        by BOTH record types as of 2026-08-14 (see Stage__c's own header, which retracts the
        old "fully disjoint" claim). The TERMINALS did not move and remain distinct, which is
        exactly what this rule relies on. Anyone re-reading Stage__c's retraction should not
        conclude this rule is now unscoped: check which value is shared before assuming.

        =====================================================================================
        TEXT(Stage__c), NEVER ISPICKVAL. RecordStageAdvanceService's class header is the
        standing repo rule for this field and the retired value 'Prepare/Review' is the
        reason: its literal slash is stored ENCODED inside a RecordType and LITERALLY
        everywhere else, so picklist comparisons on this field are done as text throughout.
        =====================================================================================

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 THE GUARD IS OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(Stage__c)) AND THE ISNEW HALF IS A DELIBERATE
        ADDITION TO WHAT THE REQUIREMENTS DOC SPECIFIED.
        =====================================================================================
        §2 A4 prescribes ISCHANGED alone, matching All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression.
        ISCHANGED IS ALWAYS FALSE ON INSERT, so ISCHANGED alone leaves a row that is CREATED
        directly at 'Executed' with no price completely unguarded. That is not a theoretical
        path: a data load, a seed script or an API caller sets Stage__c explicitly, and
        Disposition_LOI's own default is 'Received' precisely because rows are normally
        created before they are executed. Wire_Complete_Before_Sale_Closes on Disposition__c
        already uses OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(...)) for the same reason, so this shape has in
        repo precedent on the sibling gate.
        WHY A TRANSITION GUARD AT ALL, RATHER THAN THE UNGUARDED INVARIANT USED BY THE OTHER
        THREE RULES HERE: an unguarded form would freeze any PRE EXISTING Executed row that
        has no price, because every later save of it, including machine writes, would fail and
        the remedy (entering the price) would be the only permitted save. Measured today that
        population is zero, but a transition guard costs nothing and removes the freeze risk
        entirely. With the guard, an already Executed row saved for an unrelated reason is
        never blocked.

        =====================================================================================
        MEASURED IMPACT AT CREATION: ZERO ROWS. Queried on usman-dpeg, 2026-08-20:
          SELECT COUNT(Id) FROM LOI__c WHERE Stage__c = 'Executed'
                                         AND Final_Agreed_Price__c = null   -> 0
        (11 LOIs exist in total.) 🔴 That measurement ages; re-run at deploy time.
        ⚠ THE MOST LIKELY WAY A USER MEETS THIS RULE is clicking Advance Stage on a
        disposition LOI, since RecordStageAdvanceService is what moves the value. The message
        is written to be actionable from there, where the offending field may not even be on
        screen.
    -->
    <fullName>Final_Price_Required_Before_Executed</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks an LOI moving to Executed with a blank Final Agreed Price, which would propagate a null into the Opportunity Amount and the Transaction price. Names the value Executed, so it is disposition-only by construction; acquisition ends at Signed.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(Stage__c)),
    TEXT(Stage__c) = &quot;Executed&quot;,
    ISBLANK(Final_Agreed_Price__c)
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorMessage>Enter the Final Agreed Price before marking this LOI Executed. The executed price is what feeds the Opportunity amount and the transaction, so it cannot be left blank at execution.</errorMessage>
    <errorDisplayField>Final_Agreed_Price__c</errorDisplayField>
</ValidationRule>
